    rdf:value """[ Ray’s ___ life]
Tuesday, Dec. 3, 1895 
From mother’s letter: “Ray said the other day in a puzzled little tone, “Isn’t it funny, grandma, that all our life is made up of just the little things we are saying and doing all the time? I always think it is going to be some great thing, but it never is - only just the every minute little things.”
Bernhard lunched with the Buttles and took them to the Pazzi Chapel. Miss Priestley called here. In the evening we corrected the proofs of the Florentines and read Ribot’s  Heredity .
Wednesday, Dec. 4, 1895 
A nice little batch of letters - from Lippmann setting terms for the big work on Italian drawings: from Reinach arranging for a series of articles, ultimately to go into """^^xsd:string ;
